3238 0 obj
<</AP<</N 3239 0 R >>/Border[ 0 0 0]/Contents(The chief task of morphology is to understand how words are formed and how they change to convey different meanings. It's about looking at the parts of words \(like roots, prefixes, and suffixes\) to see how they fit together and create different forms and meanings. So, in your options:\n\nDeep: It's a simple word without any changes. It's like the base form.\nDeepen: This is the verb form of "deep." It's like adding something to make it stronger or more intense.\nDog: It's a singular noun, just one dog.\nDogs: This is the plural form of "dog." It means more than one dog.)/DA(/Helv 8.25 Tf 0 Tc 9.24 TL 0.8 0 0 rg )/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Rect[ 145.5 278.625 567 352.875]/Rotate 0/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
endobj
