3472 0 obj
<</AP<</N 3473 0 R >>/Border[ 0 0 0]/Contents(A morpheme is the smallest meaningful unit of language. It's like a Lego block of meaning within a word. Morphologists, who study language, look closely at words to understand:\n\nHow they are put together from smaller parts \(like roots, prefixes, and suffixes\).\nHow these parts combine to create different meanings.\nThey also explore how words change form to express different ideas, like tense or pluralization. Essentially, they dissect words to uncover their internal structure and how they are built.)/DA(/Helv 8.25 Tf 0 Tc 9.24 TL 0.8 0 0 rg )/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Rect[ 230.25 184.875 589.5 250.125]/Rotate 0/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
endobj
