<</AP<</N 4298 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(The Innateness Hypothesis proposes that humans are born with certain knowledge or abilities, rather than learning them solely from experience. In simpler terms, it suggests that some aspects of our behavior, cognition, or language are innate, meaning we have them from birth without needing to be taught. This idea suggests that certain aspects of human nature are genetically predetermined.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 4297 0 R /QuadPoints[ 84 396.25 135 396.25 84 385.25 135 385.25]/Rect[ 84 385.25 135 396.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
