<</AP<</N 4732 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(A lexeme is like the basic building block of a language's vocabulary. It's the smallest unit that carries meaning and can stand alone as a word. So, if you think about words like "play," "playing," "plays," and "played," they're all different forms of the same lexeme, which is "play." Each form might have its own ending or spelling, but they all relate to the same basic idea or concept.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 4731 0 R /QuadPoints[ 71 500.25 157 500.25 71 489.25 157 489.25]/Rect[ 71 489.25 157 500.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
