<</AP<</N 6171 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Play-ed:\nMorpheme: "play" is the root or base word, representing the action of playing. "-ed" is a suffix that indicates past tense, so "played" means the action of playing already happened in the past.\nSon-s:\nMorpheme: "son" is the root word, referring to a male child. "-s" is a suffix indicating plural, so "sons" means more than one male child.\nWait-ing:\nMorpheme: "wait" is the root word, meaning to delay or stay in expectation. "-ing" is a suffix indicating present participle or continuous action, so "waiting" means currently in the process of delaying or staying in expectation.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 6170 0 R /QuadPoints[ 84 333.25 211 333.25 84 322.25 211 322.25]/Rect[ 84 322.25 211 333.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
