<</AP<</N 13745 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(This is called overextension because they're extending the meaning of the word too far. It happens because children are still learning and figuring out the exact meanings of words. They're trying to make sense of the world around them, so they use the words they know in different situations.\nBut don't worry, this is normal! As children hear more examples of words being used correctly, like seeing big trees outside and small plants inside, they start to understand the specific meanings better. So, overextensions are usually just temporary as children learn more about language.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 13744 0 R /QuadPoints[ 169 360.25 249 360.25 169 349.25 249 349.25]/Rect[ 169 349.25 249 360.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
