<</AP<</N 16844 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents( the direct object is what the action is happening to, while the indirect object is the person or thing benefiting from the action.\nFor example, in the sentence "John gave Mary a book," "Mary" is the indirect object because she's the one receiving the book, and "a book" is the direct object because it's what is being given.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 16843 0 R /QuadPoints[ 175 411.25 298 411.25 175 400.25 298 400.25]/Rect[ 175 400.25 298 411.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
