<</AP<</N 17105 0 R >>/Border[ 0 0 0]/Contents(principle 4: Zero Allomorphs\n\nWhat it means: Sometimes, a morpheme can be represented by nothing \(zero\) if there are other forms to compare it with.\nExample:\n"fish" \(singular\) and "fish" \(plural\) … The plural form doesn't change, so it's a zero allomorph.)/DA(/Helv 8.625 Tf 0 Tc 9.66 TL 0 0.470588 0.831373 rg )/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Rect[ 240.75 48.75 606 107.25]/Rotate 0/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
