<</AP<</N 25694 0 R >>/Border[ 0 0 0]/Contents(Morphemes are the smallest meaningful units in a language. Free morphemes can stand alone as words \(Examples: "cat," "book," "run." and House", while bound morphemes must attach to other morphemes to convey meaning or perform a grammatical function \(Prefixes like "un-" in "unhappy." Suffixes like "-ed" in "played." and   suffix "-ing" in "running"\). These tiny pieces are the building blocks of words, helping to create the complex structures we use in language.)/DA(/Helv 10.5 Tf 0 Tc 11.76 TL 0 0.466667 0.831373 rg )/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Rect[ 63 56.25 554.25 115.5]/Rotate 0/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
