<</AP<</N 31864 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Principle 4: A morpheme may have zero as one of its allomorphs provided it has a non-zero allomorph. Fish generally displays no special marking in the plural: one fish, ten fish-Ø. We can say that it has a zero plural, and that this zero plural is an allomorph of the usual plural [z], because other words in the language, \nlike frogs, have non-zero plurals. This is an analytic procedure, not a theoretical point.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 31863 0 R /QuadPoints[ 86 371.25 291 371.25 86 360.25 291 360.25]/Rect[ 86 360.25 291 371.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
