42634 0 obj
<</AP<</N 42636 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Exocentricity in morphology is like a puzzle missing its main piece. Imagine you have a puzzle of a house, but one crucial piece is missing … the piece that shows the roof. Without that piece, you can't really tell it's a house anymore. In a similar way, exocentric constructions in language don't have a main part that defines what they are. For instance, think of the phrase "up and down." Each word has its own meaning, but together, they don't make a clear whole like "apple tree" or "big house." You can't replace "up" or "down" with other words and keep the same idea, showing that the phrase is exocentric.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 42635 0 R /QuadPoints[ 150 97.25 214 97.25 150 86.25 214 86.25]/Rect[ 150 86.25 214 97.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
