<</AP<</N 43040 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Sure, in simpler terms, polysemy refers to the fact that a single word can have multiple meanings. For example, the word "bank" can refer to the side of a river, a financial institution, or the act of tilting or inclining. Each of these meanings is distinct but connected by the same word. Polysemy is like having different flavors of ice cream in one scoop … it's one thing \(the word\), but it can taste different \(mean different things\) depending on the context.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 43039 0 R /QuadPoints[ 113 544.25 165 544.25 113 533.25 165 533.25]/Rect[ 113 533.25 165 544.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
