<</AP<</N 48738 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(syncretism refers to when different grammatical forms look the same. For example, in Bulgarian, the second person singular and third person singular forms in certain verb tenses are identical. they appear the same, which can create ambiguity or confusion. So, syncretism is like having two keys that look identical but open different doors … it can make it tricky to know which key to use for which door!)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 48737 0 R /QuadPoints[ 72 717.25 124 717.25 72 706.25 124 706.25]/Rect[ 72 706.25 124 717.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
