<</AP<</N 48991 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Regular inflection in nouns means that when we change the form of a noun, like making it plural, we follow specific rules that apply generally to most nouns. For example, adding "-s" or "-es" to the end of a noun to make it plural is a regular inflection rule. So, for words like "cat" and "dog," we add an "s" to make them plural: "cats" and "dogs." It's like following a recipe … you know exactly what ingredients to add and how to mix them to get the desired result!)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 48990 0 R /QuadPoints[ 441 687.25 520 687.25 441 676.25 520 676.25]/Rect[ 441 676.25 520 687.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
