49340 0 obj
<</AP<</N 49342 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Irregular inflectional plural forms are when words don't follow the usual rules for making them plural. Instead of adding "-s" or "-es" like regular plurals, these words change in unpredictable ways. For example, instead of saying "childs" for more than one child, we say "children."Similarly, we say "teeth" instead of "toothes" and "men" instead of "mans." It's like having special exceptions in a game … they don't follow the usual pattern, but we learn them because they're important!)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 49341 0 R /QuadPoints[ 84 612.25 230 612.25 84 601.25 230 601.25]/Rect[ 84 601.25 230 612.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
