<</AP<</N 50353 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Zero derivation is when a word changes its meaning or function without changing its form. This means a new word, often from a different word class, is created from an existing word, but they look exactly the same Zero-derivation changes the lexical category of a word without changing its phonological shape. For example, the noun "chair" can also be used as a verb \("to chair a meeting"\), or the noun "table" can become a verb \("to table a motion"\). It's like magic … the word transforms right before your eyes without adding or changing any letters!\n)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 50352 0 R /QuadPoints[ 119 507.25 189 507.25 119 496.25 189 496.25]/Rect[ 119 496.25 189 507.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
