<</AP<</N 51365 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(when Saussure talks about the "linguistic sign," he's saying that whenever we communicate, we're using these pairs of signifiers and signifieds to convey meaning. And sometimes, like with a stop sign, the connection between the signifier \(the red octagon\) and the signified \(stop\) is pretty clear. But with other signs, like team names, the connection might not be as obvious. That's what he meant by "motivated" and "unmotivated" signs.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 51364 0 R /QuadPoints[ 202 401.25 330 401.25 202 390.25 330 390.25]/Rect[ 202 390.25 330 401.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
