<</AP<</N 57827 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Situation 3: Take the word "unhappy." If we want to say someone is more unhappy, we might expect to add "-er" to "unhappy" to make "unhappier." But phonologically \(how the word sounds\), it's tricky because "unhappy" is already three syllables. So, instead of saying "more unhappy," we might say "less happy" to avoid the awkward sound. This creates a mismatch between what the word means and how it's formed.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 57826 0 R /QuadPoints[ 280 686.25 466 686.25 280 674.25 466 674.25]/Rect[ 280 674.25 466 686.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
