73588 0 obj
<</AP<</N 73590 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(Headed compound words are those where one part is more important than the other. This more important part is called the "head." For example, in "doghouse," "house" is the main focus, and "dog" specifies what kind of house it is. Similarly, in "notebook," the focus is on "book," with "note" describing the type of book it is. So, in short, one part leads and defines the overall meaning of the compound word.)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 73589 0 R /QuadPoints[ 84 217.25 119 217.25 84 206.25 119 206.25]/Rect[ 84 206.25 119 217.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
